{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "receiptId": "interfaces/contrast.json#contrast-round-1",
  "route": "interface-refinement",
  "briefStatus": "generation-ready",
  "authority": "agent",
  "disposition": "continue",
  "shapeVersion": "plans/spec-product.md#revision-2",
  "scopeMapVersion": "scope-map.json#mapId=preset-env-kind-map,status=approved,shapeVersion=plans/spec-product.md#revision-2",
  "decisionQuestion": "How does the Agent Presets editor expose a preset's environment kind, given that the stored value 'project-default' means a shared checkout in Stelow but a managed worktree in bb, and that the off state can only be 'BB resolves its own default' rather than a named checkout?",
  "primaryDimension": "affordance — the control shape that states (or does not overstate) where the agent works",
  "jobImportance": "Without an authorable kind there is no default at all: the request's second half (issue creation pre-filled from the preset, acceptable or changeable) has nothing to read until this field exists. The affordance is therefore the whole job, not decoration on it.",
  "fixedConstraints": [
    {
      "name": "Stored vocabulary is immutable",
      "value": "environment_kind stays 'project-default' | 'new-worktree'; the column carries a CHECK constraint and the RPC input is z.enum(...).default('project-default')",
      "source": "measured — server/preset-migrations.ts:11, server/platform-rpc-contract.ts:100"
    },
    {
      "name": "Vocabulary collision is real and measured",
      "value": "describeCardEnvironment returns 'managed' for any {type:'project-default'} and reaches 'worktree' only for host + managed-worktree, so a card on the shared-checkout path is stored 'managed', not 'shared'",
      "source": "measured — lib/tracks.mjs:94-100 (read directly this round, not inherited from the spec)"
    },
    {
      "name": "Seed, never override",
      "value": "selectCardEnvironment precedence is untouched and the card-environment.mjs:1-11 invariant survives; a human pick always wins",
      "source": "state.md shape_decisions; scope-map.json composer-seed-wiring outOfScope"
    },
    {
      "name": "Built-in presets are not editable here",
      "value": "the kind control is disabled when preset.builtIn, because flipping it cascades through firstWorktreePreset, the automation gate and defaultForm inheritance",
      "source": "scope-map.json env-kind-control; verified reachable via server/preset-lookups.ts and preset-manager-form-state.ts in the spec"
    },
    {
      "name": "No new surface, token, or design change",
      "value": "the field reuses the open form body; a new border/section or a new type step fails the recursive design-token gate",
      "source": "scope-map.json env-kind-control outOfScope; AGENTS.md UI vocabulary table"
    },
    {
      "name": "Both host files sit exactly on their debt ceilings",
      "value": "PresetManagerFormView 73/73 and PresetManagerList 74/74, neither in inheritedBaseline, so the two extractions are mandatory in the same commit",
      "source": "measured — scripts/source-debt.json:19-20, re-read this round"
    },
    {
      "name": "Touch targets and pointer are stated but untested house rules",
      "value": "min-h-11 on each clickable and cursor-pointer on the control, per AGENTS.md",
      "source": "AGENTS.md State honesty; AGENTS.md's own admission that this rule is 'stated, not tested'"
    }
  ],
  "criteria": [
    "Every state the reader can see is a promise the shipped code keeps — no label names a checkout the card will not get",
    "The control cannot be mistaken for one that does nothing; an off control must not read as broken",
    "Focus is perceivable per WCAG 2.2 on the chosen shape, verified in this repository rather than assumed",
    "The isolated-worktree vocabulary has one home, so the preset editor and the import dialog cannot drift",
    "A preset saved while a composer dialog is open cannot overwrite a human pick",
    "An unrecognised stored kind degrades to today's behaviour and says so, never throws",
    "The shape already has min-h-11 and cursor-pointer, or a test is added in the same commit",
    "The affordance is authorable in the manager form only, never on the shared assign surface"
  ],
  "relatedDimensions": [
    "vocabulary and copy ownership (who holds the words 'Isolated worktree')",
    "accessibility — focus appearance and group semantics",
    "module coupling (does the preset editor import the import dialog's concept module)",
    "scope shape (does the corrected control stay inside env-kind-control or redraw its boundary)",
    "test cost (which behaviour is pin-able without mounting the host composer)"
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "lib/tracks.mjs:94-100",
      "claim": "describeCardEnvironment({envType:'project-default'}) returns 'managed', and 'worktree' is reached only via workspaceType === 'managed-worktree'. A card started on the shared-checkout path is therefore labelled 'managed' on the card, while a preset labelled 'Project checkout' promises a shared checkout. The label and the stored fact disagree for one of the two radio states, in the direction that costs the reader most."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/creation/creation-settings.tsx:91",
      "claim": "ChoiceCards, a third in-repo radio shape the spec's reuse analysis does not mention, carries 'focus-within:outline focus-within:outline-2 focus-within:outline-primary' — the identical treatment the spec credits strategy-picker with, plus min-h-11 and cursor-pointer. The approved spec's load-bearing justification ('the strategy-picker shape is the one copied, because it is the only one in the repo that yields WCAG 2.2 focus appearance today') is therefore false: at least two shapes yield it."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/isolated-worktree-check.tsx:1-31",
      "claim": "A live on/off affordance for exactly this concept already exists and already calls itself the single source: 'Single source for the isolated-worktree concept: same words in the import dialog, the card checkout note, and the publication panel'. It exports ISOLATED_WORKTREE_LABEL, uses a checkbox with min-h-11 and cursor-pointer, and already carries the progressive-disclosure detail line. The spec named strategy-picker as the only reuse candidate and never read this file."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/github/github-import-tab.tsx:113, tests/card-start.test.mjs:150",
      "claim": "IsolatedWorktreeCheck is already mounted by the GitHub import tab and already pinned by a running test asserting the import offers 'the shared isolated toggle'. Reusing it in the preset editor would give the new control an existing consumer and an existing behavioural pin, at the cost of creating a visible reference cycle: that component's help text says 'Needs a New-worktree preset in Agent Presets', and Agent Presets would then render its words."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/settings/preset-manager-form.tsx:20,72",
      "claim": "PresetManagerFormView renders PresetExecutionPicker and nothing else; no environment-kind control exists, and environmentKind is nowhere in the file. The reported absence is literal, not a discoverability problem."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/settings/preset-manager-list.tsx:41,49,51",
      "claim": "The row's meta content sits inside a min-w-0 flex-1 truncate span while two Pills sit outside it, so an indicator added inside that span is ellipsised and never renders. The row's right edge is the only place a worktree indicator can honestly live."
    },
    {
      "source": "measured",
      "reference": "components/settings/preset-assign-options.tsx:76-88",
      "claim": "The spec's claim about this third radio shape is TRUE — a visible accent-primary radio with no focus-visible or focus-within rule. One of the spec's three reuse claims was verified correct, which is why the false one had to be re-read rather than assumed."
    },
    {
      "source": "scenario",
      "reference": "AC 4 / spec-product.md:355-360",
      "claim": "For an off preset the prop is omitted byte-for-byte and the composer's own default applies. A control that must explain the off state has to explain it in terms of BB's resolution, which is the one thing this plugin does not control and cannot keep — the off state is inexpressible as a promise, only as a mechanism."
    },
    {
      "source": "simulation",
      "reference": "reader walk-through of opt-2 vs opt-3 on the preset form",
      "claim": "On opt-2 the reader sees two labelled cards and must read the off card's sentence to learn what unchecked means. On opt-3 the reader sees one labelled checkbox; unchecked is silent by construction, so the unearned-promise failure is not solved but made structurally impossible. The cost moves to discoverability: nothing on the row explains what off does."
    },
    {
      "source": "simulation",
      "reference": "AC 9 unrecognised-kind state on each shape",
      "claim": "A fieldset+legend radio can render 'neither option selected' as an explicit third visual state with the value named in help text. A bare checkbox cannot: unrecognised and off are pixel-identical, so the explicit state has to be carried entirely by help text. This is the one criterion on which opt-3 is strictly worse than opt-2."
    },
    {
      "source": "human",
      "reference": "sw-card_cbnihg4c prompt (first reaction, recorded verbatim above)",
      "claim": "The decision-maker named two options with checkout vocabulary. No one has yet told them that one of those two words is a promise the code cannot keep, so their first reaction stands as the origin of the request and is not the shape of the answer."
    },
    {
      "source": "human",
      "reference": "gate_decision in state.md; approvals/spec-product.approved.md",
      "claim": "Review Mode is Auto with review_gates empty. The spec was approved by llm, and its own claim_verification already withdrew one unverified claim from critique round 1 — the precedent for re-reading rather than inheriting is established in this card, not imported from outside it."
    }
  ],
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "opt-2",
      "primaryValue": "Two-state radio-card, fieldset + legend, copying the strategy-picker shape, with an off-state sentence promising 'Uses BB's own default for this project'",
      "relatedValues": [
        "corrects the vocabulary collision by dropping 'Project checkout' from the reader's view while keeping project-default in storage",
        "carries the unrecognised-kind state as a visible third state (neither selected)",
        "min-h-11 and cursor-pointer must be pinned by a new test, since the house rule is stated but untested",
        "forks the isolated-worktree vocabulary away from the module that declares itself its single source"
      ],
      "compatibility": "valid"
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-3",
      "primaryValue": "On/off checkbox reusing IsolatedWorktreeCheck and ISOLATED_WORKTREE_LABEL, with the off state left silent",
      "relatedValues": [
        "eliminates the unearned-promise failure structurally rather than by careful wording",
        "inherits min-h-11 and cursor-pointer from lines 19-20, so the stated-but-untested house rule is satisfied by construction",
        "reuses a constant that already has a consumer and a running test pin (tests/card-start.test.mjs:150)",
        "creates a visible reference cycle, because the component's help text points at Agent Presets",
        "carries the benefit sentence, which describes a card rather than a preset, and has no natural home for the unrecognised-value state"
      ],
      "compatibility": "valid"
    },
    {
      "id": "opt-4",
      "primaryValue": "Two-state radio-card built on the existing ChoiceCards house style from creation-settings.tsx",
      "relatedValues": [
        "refutes the premise that opt-2 is the only accessible shape, so the choice is presented as a choice rather than a deduction",
        "consistent with the settings surfaces the preset dialog already sits next to",
        "still needs an off-state sentence, and so carries the same inexpressible-promise problem as opt-2"
      ],
      "compatibility": "valid"
    }
  ],
  "invalidOptions": [
    {
      "id": "opt-1",
      "primaryValue": "Two-option radio labelled 'Project checkout' and 'Worktree' — the decision-maker's literal first reaction",
      "why_invalid": "Not unbuildable: the storage, the RPC enum and the form union all carry it. Invalid as a reader-facing promise. lib/tracks.mjs:96 stores 'managed' for any project-default, so a card carrying a 'Project checkout' preset is labelled with a different word than the control promised. This is the exact failure the request exists to fix, and the spec reached the same conclusion for the same reason in critique gap 5. Recorded rather than dropped, because it is the request's origin and the reader deserves to see why its words changed."
    }
  ],
  "missingInputs": [
    "The decision-maker has not been shown that their own phrase 'project checkout' is the unearned promise; the vocabulary finding is recorded in state.md and the spec, never confirmed back to them. A copy pass at the interface gate should close this rather than let the change land as a silent re-labelling.",
    "No reader test distinguishes opt-2 from opt-3: no first-reader pass has said whether a checkbox with a silent off state is understood as 'off = BB decides' or read as 'not set up yet'. The contrast rests on structure, not on observed comprehension.",
    "Whether the visible reference cycle created by opt-3 is acceptable to the person who wrote the isolated-worktree module is unasked; the cycle is a copy question, and the module's comment shows the words are deliberately centralised."
  ],
  "acceptedSacrifice": "Accept, under opt-3, that the preset editor's control is a bare checkbox rather than a grouped fieldset: the off state gets no sentence at all, so a reader who has never seen the form learns nothing about what off does, and the unrecognised-kind state (AC 9) is carried by help text alone. Both are accepted because the off state is the pre-existing behaviour, because explaining it is what forced the unearned promise in the first place, and because a card that lands where BB's own default put it is not a defect to be warned about. The cost is paid in discoverability, deliberately, to buy a control that cannot lie.",
  "reshapeProof": null,
  "nextAction": "Coordinator: the primary decision is settled by evidence and needs no human boundary, but scope-map.json env-kind-control pins the displaced choice by name — its inScope line reads 'copying components/creation/strategy-picker.tsx:64-104, the only in-repo radio shape yielding WCAG 2.2 focus appearance today', and that clause is false. Emit scope-map-challenge.json (do not edit the approved map) proposing: (a) keep the on/off primary value, which the evidence strengthens; (b) replace the copy target with IsolatedWorktreeCheck/ISOLATED_WORKTREE_LABEL and record the reference cycle and the silent off state as named costs; (c) add the newly verified ChoiceCards focus treatment to the spec's reuse analysis so the false uniqueness claim is corrected at source, not only in this receipt; (d) carry the three missingInputs into the interface gate, the first of which needs the decision-maker shown why 'project checkout' did not survive. Then hand the interface pick to the canonical selection stage — this receipt records the contrast, it does not own the selection."
}
